  "phase3_gemini_self_healing": {
    "forensics": "The losing cluster is heavily driven by a low-conviction 1.3x volume sweep threshold triggering mid-day false breakouts (notably a 5-loss long cluster on 2026-10-22 against broader market weakness) and tight 0.40% initial stops getting whipsawed by normal 5-minute NSE intraday noise. Furthermore, trades #5 and #8 on TATASTEEL reached the 1.0R breakeven trigger and exited with small gross profits (\u20b93.36), but flipped into net losses due to statutory transaction fees (~\u20b93.98 per trade), resulting in nearly 100% of the cycle's \u20b9-45.51 net loss being attributable to \u20b945.35 in fee drag.",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE cash equities on a \u20b910,000 capital base, statutory brokerage and STT/exchange charges create a ~0.15% round-trip hurdle that turns tight-stop breakeven scratches and low-volume midday sweeps into systematic negative-expectancy bleed; survival requires high-conviction institutional volume confirmation (>2.0x) and wider structural stops/targets to amortize fixed transaction costs.",
    "parameter_patch": {
      "min_target_pct": 1.25,
      "min_sweep_vol_multiplier": 2.1,
      "breakeven_trigger_r": 1.25,
      "min_sl_pct": 0.55
    },
    "plan_update_summary": "### Cycle #19 Post-Mortem & Parameter Evolution\nForensic analysis of Cycle #19 revealed severe fee drag (\u20b945.35 in fees vs \u20b9-45.51 Net P&L) and midday false-positive sweeps (5 correlated long losses on Oct 22). A permissive `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` of 1.3x allowed low-liquidity noise to trigger entries during the 11:00\u201313:45 IST lull, while a tight `min_sl_pct` of 0.40% and `breakeven_trigger_r` of 1.0R caused premature stop-outs and fee-negative breakeven scratches (e.g., TATASTEEL trades #5 and #8). For Cycle #20, we are tightening institutional participation filters by raising `min_sweep_vol_multiplier` to **2.1x**, widening `min_sl_pct` to **0.55%** to clear 5-minute microstructure noise, expanding `min_target_pct` to **1.25%** to overcome NSE statutory fee drag, and pushing `breakeven_trigger_r` to **1.25R** to prevent premature profit choking."
  },
